{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"source": "data\\documents\\pdf\\Fiona Stanley Hospital Dermatology-Psoriasis-guidelines-2025.pdf", "filename": "Fiona Stanley Hospital Dermatology-Psoriasis-guidelines-2025.pdf", "filepath": "data\\documents\\pdf\\Fiona Stanley Hospital Dermatology-Psoriasis-guidelines-2025.pdf", "page": 3, "title": "FSH Dermatology Psoriasis Guidelines", "year": "2025", "producer": "Adobe PDF Library 21.5.90", "creator": "Acrobat PDFMaker 21 for Word", "creationdate": "2025-05-20T10:40:48+08:00", "author": "Fiona Stanley Hospital Dermatology", "company": "WA Health", "contenttypeid": "0x010100D20558782E22444F8E6476743C0A7A47", "keywords": "Fiona Stanley Hospital, FSH, dermatology, pre-referral guidelines, psoriasis", "moddate": "2025-05-20T10:40:49+08:00", "sourcemodified": "D:20250520024043", "subject": "Information on referring, treament and introduction to Psoriasis", "_dlc_dociditemguid": "400bd398-572f-4117-a0d8-763933fbd180", "total_pages": 5, "page_label": "4"}, "page_content": "Dermatology pre-referral guidelines \u2013 Psoriasis May2025 Page 4 of 5 \n* PBS approved for chronic stable plaque type psoriasis vulgaris that is inadequately controlled by \npotent topical corticosteroid monotherapy. \nOther treatments may be used at the hospital \n\u2022 Phototherapy. \n\u2022 Systemic agents: Methotrexate, Acitretin, Cyclosporin, Apremilast. \n\u2022 Biologic therapy is reserved for severe psoriasis and/or psoriatic psoriasis that has failed to \nrespond to conventional systemic therapy. There are many biologic agents currently \navailable on the PBS - https://www.servicesaustralia.gov.au/psoriasis-severe-chronic-\nplaque-psoriasis?context=20  \nWhen to refer \nIf the diagnosis is unclear, or if there are ongoing signs or symptoms which remain problematic \ndespite the above management, please refer to the\u202fDermatology Department.  \nEssential information to include in your referral \n\u2022 Duration of psoriasis. \n\u2022 Affected sites. \n\u2022 Estimation of body surface area involved \u2013 this may help us triage urgency of referral. \n\u2022 Previous and current treatment, and how long this was used for. \n\u2022 Associated psoriatic nail disease and psoriatic arthritis. \n\u2022 Co-morbidities and current medications.", "type": "Document"}}